          "to": "ddukeř",
          "note": "Riffian ⟨ř⟩ is the reflex of singleton *l; in most Western and Central dialects it has merged with original r, and where the two stay apart ř is a trill [r] while original r is a tap. Kabyle and Mzab keep l (alwes, alili). Geminate *ll gives ǧ [dʒː] and *lt gives č [tʃ] instead; the easternmost dialects (Icebdanen, Iznasen) do not take part."
